INT. DIVING BELL - CHANNEL FLOOR, 1861

A riveted iron bell, six feet across. Two brass portholes. A hissing air hose. Green water presses against the glass. A candle burns in a sealed lantern.

ARCHIBALD PENHALLOW (50s, engineer, mutton-chop whiskers) crouches at the air valve. DR. TOBIAS FENWICK (40s, naturalist, spectacles fogged) clutches a specimen jar. CORNELIUS VANE (30s, company agent, pinstripe suit ruined by damp) sits rigid on the bench.

ARCHIBALD
Forty feet. Pressure steady.

TOBIAS
Marvelous. Marvelous. Look at the light.

CORNELIUS
I am looking at the water, Doctor. It is looking back.

ARCHIBALD
Keep your voice down. Sound travels.

CORNELIUS
Where would it travel to?

ARCHIBALD
The surface. Where the men on the pump are listening for trouble.

A tap on the glass. All three look. A pale fish, huge and slow, drifts past.

TOBIAS
Lophius. Oh, Cornelius, you must see this.

CORNELIUS
I have no wish to see it.

TOBIAS
It's a monkfish. A giant.

He holds up the jar. Fogs the porthole with his breath. Wipes it. He leans so close his nose touches the glass.

ARCHIBALD
Get back from the window.

TOBIAS
It's only a fish.

ARCHIBALD
It's the pressure on the glass I'm worried about.

CORNELIUS
You said it was safe.

ARCHIBALD
I said it was safe if we keep still.

The bell shudders. A low groan from the iron seams. The candle gutters.

CORNELIUS
What was that?

ARCHIBALD
The sea settling.

TOBIAS
Is it settling, or moving?

ARCHIBALD
Be quiet. Both of you.

He unhooks a speaking tube and listens. Nothing. He taps it. Nothing.

ARCHIBALD (CONT'D)
The line's dead.

CORNELIUS
Then we're lost.

ARCHIBALD
We are not lost. The pump men have a signal. Three tugs on the cord.

He seizes the cord. Pulls three times. Waits. Pulls again.

Silence. Tobias lowers the jar. His hand trembles. He sets it on the floor.

TOBIAS
I have always wanted to die in the name of science. I merely hadn't pictured it so damp.

CORNELIUS
Doctor, please.

ARCHIBALD
Nobody is dying. Cornelius, hand me that wrench.

CORNELIUS
This one?

ARCHIBALD
The long one.

Cornelius passes it. Archibald hammers the iron wall. Once. Twice. Three times. A pause.

Three muffled knocks answer from above. All three exhale at once.

TOBIAS
They heard.

ARCHIBALD
They always hear.

The bell lurches. Rises. Slowly. The water in the porthole begins to lighten from green to gray.

CORNELIUS
Archibald?

ARCHIBALD
Yes?

CORNELIUS
When we are up, I intend to be sick.

ARCHIBALD
Hold on to the bench.
